{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline","id":346003,"title":"Dead Wolf - Bloodline","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-20T12:12:39-08:00","id":346003,"title":"Dead Wolf - Bloodline","content":"I noticed that no one has done a write up for this and I think they are a very interesting bloodline. This is what I have come up with so far in my brain storming. I do not think it is appropriate to allow them to take werewolf forms other than the basic wolf form protean already allows.<br /> <br /> <b>__________________________________________________ ___________________________________<br /> <br /> Bloodline Bane:</b> Dead Wolves suffer from a vulnerability of their blood. Any damage inflicted on a Dead Wolf with a silver weapon deals lethal damage. This also counts as a bane when determining things such as the use of Resilience.<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline Disciplines:</b> Animalism, Auspex, Protean, Resilience<br /> <br /> <b>Luna\u2019s Gift</b><br /> Is granted to Dead Wolves when they join the bloodline. It is not directly granted to them, but soaked up from Luna\u2019s ambient grace by power of the Dead Wolf\u2019s Blood and offers a number of benefits.<ul><li>Allows the dead wolf to purchase dots in the Totem merit to contribute to a pack totem with werewolves and to receive the benefits and drawbacks of this merit. They are still unable to use gifts.</li> </ul><ul><li>Purchase the Sublunario merit, which is exclusive to the bloodline.</li> </ul><ul><li>When joining the bloodline they choose a moon phase: Full, Gibbous, Half, Crescent or New, which allows them to ride the wave with no willpower cost during the selected moon phase. This also determines some of the benefits they receive with Sublunario and potentially how Werewolves interact with them based on moon phase.</li> </ul><ul><li>Allows them access to rites and fetish use. Dead Wolves count as werewolves for purposes of use or effect when using rites or a fetish. Any cost in essence is paid in twice the cost essence.</li> </ul><ul><li>Purchasing cost for rite rating 4 per dot and 2 per rite.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><u>Sublunario</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b><ul><li>May add Sublunario rating as a bonus to ride the wave, regardless of moon phase.</li> <li>Use Sublunario rating in place of Harmony when using Rites or Activating a fetish.</li> </ul><br /> <b>Active: </b>By spending a point of Vitae and an instant action the dead wolf may divide their Sublunario rating as bonus dice between the three Insight Skills that are linked with their chosen moon phase. These bonus dice can be split between the three skills any way they see fit and last until the end of the scene. If the character wishes to reassign this bonus in the same scene, they must spend another Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Insight Skills</b><br /> Full Moon (Warrior): Brawl, Intimidation, Survival<br /> Gibbous Moon (Visionary): Crafts, Expression, Persuasion<br /> Half Moon (Walker Between): Empathy, Investigation, Politics<br /> Crescent Moon (Spirit Master): Animal Ken, Medicine, Occult<br /> New Moon (Stalker): Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T14:11:48-08:00","id":346085,"title":"","content":"Well technically BS Protean at level 4 could allow them to imitate the various werewolf forms by activating different animal aspects at the same time. Wolf head (for enhanced smelling and vision capabilities and teeth) + bear skin (armor) and lion legs (for claws and running) could result in a pretty grotesque chimera that superficially resembles one of the different werewolf forms. Of course they don't get the benefit of generating Lunacy or whatever their deus ex machina effect they get which forces normal human minds to not register that they're seeing a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Personally I rather liked the idea of this bloodline but why are they getting Auspex? Sublunario could be a scalable merit chain that lets them do things like craft and use werewolf specific fetishes, or see and communicate with a totem spirit they can attune with, learn werewolf rituals and maybe convert vitae to essence in a limited fashion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","user":"Audrey St. John","date":". 12-20-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T15:43:59-08:00","id":346200,"title":"","content":"Werewolf 2e will be out before too long (it's in layout at the moment), and will sufficiently change up things like how rites work that you may want to do a second draft of this after its release. In particular, the new Wolf-Blooded rules might offer some interesting ideas to plunder for the bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-20T17:23:19-08:00","id":346246,"title":"","content":"With the thematics of auspex in 2e I dont think it's a suitable choice for the bloodline. Bloodline gift is a little too potent, I think, too. Still, glad to see someone tackling dead wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T17:30:17-08:00","id":347075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=346246#post346246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the thematics of auspex in 2e I dont think it's a suitable choice for the bloodline. Bloodline gift is a little too potent, I think, too. Still, glad to see someone tackling dead wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't worried about balance at all when making the merits. Right now it is simply brainstorming with ideas of what potentially could fit where.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T17:31:15-08:00","id":347076,"title":"","content":"As far as Auspex goes, it felt like the best fit. Auspex is great for hunting things that normal vision cannot see as well as finding their weakness. This is something Werewolves have to contend with all the time, and by Proxy a Dead Wolf that hunts with them. Put simply you can't hunt what you can't find or see and you can't kill something you don't know how to kill.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or perhaps they are limited to 3 disciplines and can do rites as an affinity?<br /> <br /> I see this bloodline as having more of a spiritual connection, rather than being murder machines or bending others will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","user":"Maskah","date":". 12-21-2014, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T17:38:50-08:00","id":347078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=346085#post346085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well technically BS Protean at level 4 could allow them to imitate the various werewolf forms by activating different animal aspects at the same time. Wolf head (for enhanced smelling and vision capabilities and teeth) + bear skin (armor) and lion legs (for claws and running) could result in a pretty grotesque chimera that superficially resembles one of the different werewolf forms. Of course they don't get the benefit of generating Lunacy or whatever their deus ex machina effect they get which forces normal human minds to not register that they're seeing a werewolf.<br /> <br /> Personally I rather liked the idea of this bloodline but why are they getting Auspex? Sublunario could be a scalable merit chain that lets them do things like craft and use werewolf specific fetishes, or see and communicate with a totem spirit they can attune with, learn werewolf rituals and maybe convert vitae to essence in a limited fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Protean 4 only lets you change certain aspects, like having wings, or growing claws for example. You can only have 1 lvl 4 aspect readied at any given time. Level 4 does not cover full on shape changing, only level 3 does and it is specific to Predatory and Carrion animals only. It would be OP to allow vampires to take werewolf forms considering what they can do now in 2nd ED. Even if you were getting just the stat boost you would still be better off taking animal forms since those also provide a physical skill adjustment.<br /> <br /> I think simply allowing the Dead Wolves to purchase Totem and Fetish Merits as a basic bloodline gift it fine and should not require another merit to do so.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T17:42:09-08:00","id":347079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=346200#post346200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Werewolf 2e will be out before too long (it's in layout at the moment), and will sufficiently change up things like how rites work that you may want to do a second draft of this after its release. In particular, the new Wolf-Blooded rules might offer some interesting ideas to plunder for the bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea I am pretty excited about that book coming out. I am sure that I will have to come back an edit my draft for the dead wolves.<br /> <br /> I also pondered making this bloodline something only wolf blooded become when they get embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1852,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","user":"Maskah","date":". 12-21-2014, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-21T20:04:23-08:00","id":347120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maskah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=347078#post347078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Protean 4 only lets you change certain aspects, like having wings, or growing claws for example. You can only have 1 lvl 4 aspect readied at any given time. Level 4 does not cover full on shape changing, only level 3 does and it is specific to Predatory and Carrion animals only.</div> </div> </div> </div>At level 2 you can use three different predatory aspects at a time. At level 4 you gain a forth one which can be used in conjunction with the first three and is considered a manifestation of the protean user's Beast.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; It would be OP to allow vampires to take werewolf forms considering what they can do now in 2nd ED. Even if you were getting just the stat boost you would still be better off taking animal forms since those also provide a physical skill adjustment. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Personally I'm disinclined to allow vampires to gain the full benefit of the various werewolf forms because they're vampires, not werewolves. I pointed it out because giving them the ability to adopt the generic benefits of the werewolf forms would be a rather redundant ability since they can already do so via Protean. (I might consider the possibility of the more overt supernatural enhancements if said vampire eats a werewolf but that's another matter altogether.)<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; As far as Auspex goes, it felt like the best fit. Auspex is great for hunting things that normal vision cannot see as well as finding their weakness. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Auspex does not grant heightened senses anymore. That is the purview of Kindred Senses, which all kindred get by default, and the Acute Senses merit, which any kindred can buy. Auspex is now a line of sight psychic fear detection power with a variant of Dominate 4's memory alteration power and some astral projection and psychometry added in, just because.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/190-audrey-st-john","name":"Audrey St. John","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T20:33:38-08:00","id":349491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Audrey St. John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=347120#post347120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At level 2 you can use three different predatory aspects at a time. At level 4 you gain a forth one which can be used in conjunction with the first three and is considered a manifestation of the protean user's Beast.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; It would be OP to allow vampires to take werewolf forms considering what they can do now in 2nd ED. Even if you were getting just the stat boost you would still be better off taking animal forms since those also provide a physical skill adjustment. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Personally I'm disinclined to allow vampires to gain the full benefit of the various werewolf forms because they're vampires, not werewolves. I pointed it out because giving them the ability to adopt the generic benefits of the werewolf forms would be a rather redundant ability since they can already do so via Protean. (I might consider the possibility of the more overt supernatural enhancements if said vampire eats a werewolf but that's another matter altogether.)<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; As far as Auspex goes, it felt like the best fit. Auspex is great for hunting things that normal vision cannot see as well as finding their weakness. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> Auspex does not grant heightened senses anymore. That is the purview of Kindred Senses, which all kindred get by default, and the Acute Senses merit, which any kindred can buy. Auspex is now a line of sight psychic fear detection power with a variant of Dominate 4's memory alteration power and some astral projection and psychometry added in, just because.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am aware of the aspects that they give and I am only basing any thoughts I have off what is listed in the book specifically.<br /> <br /> Still for other reasons of pinpointing weakness in a target Auspex is very valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-24T20:40:19-08:00","id":349492,"title":"","content":"Honestly I do not think it is worth the effort to convert this bloodline. Between Coil of Ziritra and the new wolf blooded merits, which would also let you use a fetish and invest in totems. Apparently some of those wolf blooded merits can allow you to take some of the forms, but there are draw backs in taking those merits so it balances out.<br /> <br /> <br /> I actually see the dead wolves as a faction within the Ordo that have reclaimed their connection to the wolf.<br /> <br /> If anything Sublunario can be changed to be specific to that faction and act as such.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Sublunario</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Persistent:</b><ul><li>May add Sublunario rating as a bonus to ride the wave, regardless of moon phase.</li> </ul><b>Active: </b>By spending a point of Vitae and an instant action the dead wolf may divide their Sublunario rating as bonus dice between the three Insight Skills that are linked with their chosen moon phase. These bonus dice can be split between the three skills any way they see fit and last until the end of the scene. If the character wishes to reassign this bonus in the same scene, they must spend another Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Insight Skills</b><br /> Full Moon (Warrior): Brawl, Intimidation, Survival<br /> Gibbous Moon (Visionary): Crafts, Expression, Persuasion<br /> Half Moon (Walker Between): Empathy, Investigation, Politics<br /> Crescent Moon (Spirit Master): Animal Ken, Medicine, Occult<br /> New Moon (Stalker): Larceny, Stealth, Subterfuge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1852-maskah","name":"Maskah","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T18:53:49-07:00","id":433405,"title":"","content":"Bringing this thread back up, I'd love to see an official rework of them in honor of WtF 2e. Any chance Rose or David might be coaxed into it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:15:17-07:00","id":433503,"title":"","content":"I think an easy way to go about it now would be to just effectively give them the wolf blood template. Not directly, but their gift gives them a Tell, the ability to buy Totem if accepted into a Pack (and only then), and the ability to use Pack Rites. Loses some of the original sublunario flavor, but I think suits the bloodline itself better, since they were originally meant to be wolf blooded and all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T22:35:15-07:00","id":433607,"title":"","content":"Incidentally, it does say a Wolf-blooded <i>does not </i>lose their Tell if they get turned into another supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T23:04:24-07:00","id":433616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=433607#post433607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, it does say a Wolf-blooded <i>does not </i>lose their Tell if they get turned into another supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also true. Should probably have it note that they only gain one if they didn't already have one (But it might be a good excuse to buy the Tell merit for another)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T23:53:01-07:00","id":435388,"title":"","content":"Since Tells are no longer lost upon Embrace, why don't we make this a Lodge instead of a Bloodline? That way, it's not just Gangrel who can join.<br /> <br /> <b>Lodge of Dead Wolves</b><br /> Though the stories say that Juan Colmillo was the first Dead Wolf, enough Wolf-Blooded have been embraced prior to their First Change that they've started a Lodge in imitation of the Uratha. <br /> <br /> <b>Prerequisites</b>: All members of the Lodge must be Wolf-Blooded who have been embraced. Furthermore, they must also be part of an active werewolf pack. The goal of the Lodge is to equip the Dead Wolves to assist in the Siskur-Dah.<br /> <br /> <b>Benefit</b>: I recommend using the Blood Tenebrous from the Book of Spirits. That way, the Dead Wolves can aid in the hunt through the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T02:29:48-07:00","id":435496,"title":"","content":"So it works as a sort of all-comers pseudo-bloodline? <br /> <br /> I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:22:09-07:00","id":435718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435496#post435496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So it works as a sort of all-comers pseudo-bloodline?<br /> I like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like a Covenant for vampires who largely abandon Kindred society for the sake of the pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:37:31-07:00","id":435754,"title":"","content":"Do you think being a major template should net them the 3 dot Pack Bond merit automatically or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:03:45-07:00","id":435769,"title":"","content":"That lodge sounds more like a separate thing from what Dead wolves are, as the whole point of Dead Wolves is that the wolf nature is in their blood.<br /> <br /> That said, I think if you renamed it the two would go really well hand in hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:33:55-07:00","id":435829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435769#post435769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That lodge sounds more like a separate thing from what Dead wolves are, as the whole point of Dead Wolves is that the wolf nature is in their blood.<br /> That said, I think if you renamed it the two would go really well hand in hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Maybe I'll invent a patron for them among the Wolf Brothers so they can be a proper lodge. Sanguine Wolf, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:43:52-07:00","id":435836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435769#post435769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole point of Dead Wolves is that the wolf nature is in their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>But these are wolf blooded vampires so it sort of, well, <i>is</i>. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T09:55:19-07:00","id":435850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435829#post435829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point. Maybe I'll invent a patron for them among the Wolf Brothers so they can be a proper lodge. Sanguine Wolf, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Something like that could work pretty decently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435836#post435836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But these are wolf blooded vampires so it sort of, well, <i>is</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but my point is that the connection IS the blood, there's no real gatherings for them or organization. It's a more primal connection, and that just says gangrel bloodline to me, not a lodge of former wolf bloods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T11:15:51-07:00","id":435983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point. Maybe I'll invent a patron for them among the Wolf Brothers so they can be a proper lodge. Sanguine Wolf, perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodthirsty Wolf? Red-Maw Wolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T16:24:47-07:00","id":439025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>falco1029</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/346003-dead-wolf-bloodline?p=435850#post435850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but my point is that the connection IS the blood, there's no real gatherings for them or organization. It's a more primal connection, and that just says gangrel bloodline to me, not a lodge of former wolf bloods.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. Yes, the dead wolves are heavily tied to werewolves, but they shouldn't be tied down to a Lodge if they don't want to be. While the Dead Wolves are supposed to add to vampire/werewolf crossovers, they are vampires first and should be able to run solo. On top of all that, it just feels wrong for them not to have Protean. I think Maskah had the right idea even if it came too soon.<br /> <br /> I don't know what extra Discipline I would give them, but I would probably make their Bloodline Gift Sublunario, which would let them choose a moon phase. On nights when that moon was in the sky they would gain a point of Willpower the first time they looked at the moon at night and the ability to ride the wave for free. They would also gain the hunter's aspect (werewolf predatory aura) of their moon phase and the ability to purchase dots in the Totem Merit.<br /> <br /> If the Dead Wolves were done in a way like I just did, then they would gain a bunch of stuff that would make them better vampires, not just some werewolf wannabes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T13:05:40-07:00","id":575530,"title":"","content":"So I'm planning to use this bloodline for my W:tF game, as one of my players plays one and it wants to join our pack. We know our player will have a Tell, formerly being a Wolf-Blood. The thing is we don't know how to update it's discipline: Sublunario, correctly. Also my player wants the Dead Wolves bloodline to know all the Uratha's five forms. In 1st ed the devotion wolfman: Protean 3 and Sublunario 3 made Dalu form but now we can just use protean 4 for that, as for Urhan form we have protean 3. For Gauru and Urshul we were thinking of making it into a devotion, of course.<br /> <br /> With the bloodline's help...<br /> War Form or Shape of the Beast's Wrath (V:tM)<br /> Protean 4 and Sublunario 4<br /> Cost: 5 vitae<br /> Same benefits as Gauru except rage is replace by frenzy<br /> <br /> Near wolf form or Savage Hound<br /> Protean 3 and Sublunario 3<br /> Cost: 3 or 4 vitae<br /> Same benefits as Urshul except rage is replace by frenzy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}